                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Extract from the El Paso Herald dated July 26,
                        1001.</hi></head>
                <p>Ambassador Clayton could learn more about the men in jail if he would only send
                    some one to Jalapa, Orizaba, Veracruz, and Oaxaca. There are 130 men in jail in
                    these four places, and some of them have been there for two years. The records
                    in some of the cases have been lost, and I know of several men there who have
                    repeatedly asked for trial and been refused.</p>
            </div>
